G'day all,

First an admission: I'm new to Linux, so I may be overlooking something very simple, but I'm having trouble with the compile. I've tried the install through GitHub using both the devtools package and the githubinstall package from within R, and they both run into an inappropriate ELF. Seems like the version on git was built on a 64 bit platform, and I'm running a 32bit system.

Any advice on how to build a 32bit compile would be helpful. I've found ways to do this from the Debian commandline, but I'm unsure about how to compile in an appropriate place for R to find the package. Knowing my luck I'll compile NicheMapR somewhere silly and never be able to find it again.

Cheers

Sean Tomlinson

